hadiths[232]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3724","Narrated 'Ali:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I am the house of wisdom"""
"3725","**Narrated by al-Ansari, Ishaq ibn Musa narrated to us; Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us; al-Zuhri narrated to me from 'Urwah from 'Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), who said:**\n\n\The first thing with which the Prophethood of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commenced"
"3726","Narrated Al-Bara:\The Prophet (ﷺ) dispatched two armies and put 'Ali bin Abi Talib in charge of one of them"""
"3727","Narrated Jabir:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called 'Ali on the Day (of the battle) of At-Ta'if"""
"3728","Narrated Abu Sa'eed:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to 'Ali: \O 'Ali! It is not permissible for anyone to be Junub in this Masjid except for you and I"""
"3729","Narrated Anas bin Malik:\The advent of the Prophet (ﷺ) was on Monday and 'Ali performed Salat on Tuesday"""
"3730","Narrated Ali:\When I would ask the Messenger of Allah SAW he would give me"""
"3731","Abu Ja'far, Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Abi Halimah from Qasr al-Ahnaf, and Ahmad ibn Abda al-Dabbi, and Ali ibn Hujr — the meaning is one — they said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us: Umar ibn Abd Allah, mawla of Ghufrah, narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from the descendants of Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) when describing the Prophet ﷺ said: He was not the tall, lanky (al-mumaghat), nor the short, stunted (al-mutarradid); he was of medium stature among people (rab'ah). He was not extremely curly (al-j'ad al-qatat) nor straight-haired (al-sabit); he was wavy-haired (j'ad rajil). He was not fleshy-cheeked (al-mutahhim) nor round-faced (al-mukaltham). There was roundness in his face, white mixed with redness (mushrab), his eyes were intensely black with a tinge of blue (ad'aj), his eyelashes were long (ahdab), his shoulder joints and upper back (al-katid) were large. He was hairless (ajrad) except for a line of fine hair (al-masrubah) from his chest to his navel. His hands and feet were thick-fingered (shathn). When he walked, he walked briskly (taqalla'a) as if descending a slope (sabab). When he turned, he turned fully (together). Between his shoulders was the Seal of Prophethood, and he is the Seal of the Prophets. He was the most generous of people in hand, the most open of them in chest, the most truthful of them in speech, the softest of them in temperament, and the noblest of them in companionship. Whoever saw him suddenly (badihah) was awed by him, and whoever mixed with him knowingly loved him. The one describing him says: I have not seen before him nor after him the like of him. Abu Isa said: This is a Hasan Gharib hadith; its chain is not connected. Abu Ja'far said: I heard al-Asma'i say in his interpretation of the description of the Prophet ﷺ: al-mumaghat means going to extreme in height. And I heard a Bedouin say: tamaghghata in a bow, meaning he stretched it a severe stretch. As for al-mutarradid, it is that which enters some into some in shortness. As for al-qatat, it is the intense curliness; and al-rajil is he in whose hair there is slight waviness. As for al-mutahhim, it is the corpulent, abundant in flesh. As for al-mukaltham, it is the round-faced. As for al-mushrab, it is that in whose whiteness there is redness. Al-ad'aj is the intensely black-eyed. Al-ahdab is the long-eyelashed. Al-katid is the junction of the two shoulders, and it is the upper back (al-kahil). Al-masrubah is the fine hair that is like a rod from the chest to the navel. Al-shathn is the thick fingers of the hands and feet. Al-taqalla' is to walk with strength. Al-sabab is the descent; he says: we descended in a sabub and sabab. His saying ""jalil al-mushash"" means the heads of the shoulders. Al-ashirah is companionship, and al-ashir is the companion. Al-badihah is the sudden surprise; it is said: badahtuhu bi-amr, meaning I surprised him with a matter."
"3732","Narrated Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said to 'Ali"
"3733","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\The Prophet (ﷺ) ordered that the gates be closed"""
"3734","Qutaybah narrated to us, Ibn Luha‘iyyah narrated to us, from ‘Ubaydullah ibn al-Mughirah, from ‘Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz’, who said: \I have not seen anyone smile more than the Messenger of Allah"
"3735","It has been narrated from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb, from ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Jazʾ, a similar narration.\n\nAḥmad ibn Khālid al-Khallāl related to us, he said: Yaḥyā ibn Isḥāq al-Saylaḥānī related to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Saʿd related to us, from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb, from ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Jazʾ, who said:\n\n\The Messenger of Allah ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam never laughed except by way of a smile (tafakkuh/tabassum).\""\n\nAbū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) commented: *\""This is a ṣaḥīḥ (authentic) gharīb (uncommon/singular) ḥadīth. We do not know it from the ḥadīth of Layth ibn Saʿd except through this chain (wajh).\""*"

"\n- **Abū ʿĪsā** refers to Imām Abū ʿĪsā Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī (رحمه الله)"""
"3736","Narrated a man from the Ansar:that Zaid bin Al-Arqam said: \The first to accept Islam was 'Ali.\"" 'Amr bin Murrah said: \""So I mentioned that to Ibrahim An-Nakha'i"""
"3737","Narrated 'Ali:\The Prophet (ﷺ) - the Unlettered Prophet - exhorted me (saying): 'None loves you except a believer and none hates you except a hypocrite.'\"" 'Adi bin Thabit (a narrator) said: \""I am from the generation whom the Prophet (ﷺ) supplicated for"""
"3738","Narrated Umm 'Atiyyah:\The Prophet (ﷺ) sent an army in which was 'Ali.\"" She said: \""While he was raising his hands"""
"3739","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Az-Zubair:that Az-Zubair said: \On the Day of (the battle of) Uhud"""
"3740","Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever would be pleased to look at a martyr walking upon the face of the earth"""
"3741","Narrated Musa bin Talhah:\I entered upon Mu'awiyah and he said: 'Shall I not give you some good news?' I said: 'Of course!' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'Talhah is among those who fulfilled their vow (referring to 33:)"""
"3742","Narrated 'Ali bin abi Talib:\My ear heard from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"""
"3743","Narrated by Ahmad ibn Mani' and Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawriqi, who both said: Isma'il ibn 'Ulayyah narrated to us from Khalid al-Khadda', who said: 'Ammar, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to me that he heard Ibn 'Abbas"
"3744","Narrated by **Nasr ibn Ali al-Jahdami**, who said: **Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal** narrated to us, who said: **Khalid al-Hadhdha'** narrated to us, who said: **Ammar**, the freed slave of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, who said: **Ibn Abbas** (may Allah be pleased with him) informed us that the Prophet (peace be upon him) passed away at the age of sixty-five.\n\n**Abu Isa** (Imam al-Tirmidhi) said: This is a **hasan** (good) and **sahih** (authentic) hadith with a sound chain of narration."
"3745","Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib [may Allah be pleased with him]:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"""
"3746","Narrated Jabir [may Allah be pleased with him]:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"""
"3747","Narrated Hisham bin 'Urwah:\On the Day of (the battle of) Al-Jamal"""
"3748","Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Awf:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Abu Bakr is in Paradise"""
"3749","It was narrated to us by Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari, who said: It was narrated to us by Isma'il ibn Abi Uwais, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'Aisha, from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: Abu Bakr was our master, our best, and the most beloved of us to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). Abu 'Isa [al-Tirmidhi] said: This is a sahih (authentic) gharib (uncommon) hadith."
"3750","Narrated Abu Salamah:from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say: \Indeed your affair [feminine plural: referring to the wives of the Prophet (ﷺ)] is from that which concerns me after me"""
"3751","Narrated Abu Salamah:that 'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Awf left a garden for the Mothers of the Believers that was sold for four-hundred thousand"
"3752","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Shawarib narrated to us: Abu Awanah narrated to us from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ibn Abi al-Mu'alla, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave a sermon one day and said: ""Indeed a man was given a choice by his Lord between living in this world as long as he wished to live and eating in this world whatever he wished to eat, and meeting his Lord; so he chose meeting his Lord."" Abu Bakr wept. The Companions of the Prophet ﷺ said: ""Do you not wonder at this old man? When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned a righteous man whom his Lord gave a choice between the world and meeting his Lord, he chose meeting his Lord."" Abu Bakr was the most knowledgeable of them about what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ meant. Abu Bakr said: ""Rather we ransom you with our fathers and our wealth."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""There is no one among people more secure to us in his companionship and his wealth than Ibn Abi Quhafah. And if I were to take a close friend (khalil), I would have taken Ibn Abi Quhafah as a khalil. But (it is) affection and brotherhood of faith, affection and brotherhood of faith"" — two or three times. ""And indeed your companion is the Khalil of Allah."" This hadith has been narrated from Abu Awanah from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr with a chain other than this. The meaning of his saying ""amanna ilayna"" is: he is most trustworthy/secure over us. In the chapter there is also from Abu Sa'id. And this is a Hasan Gharib hadith."
"3753","**Narrated by Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī (may Allāh be pleased with him):**\n\nThe Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) ascended the pulpit and said:\n\n> \Indeed"
"3754","Narrated 'Ali:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not mention both (his) parents for anyone except Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas. On the Day of (the battle of) Uhud he said: 'Shoot"""
"3755","Narrated Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) mentioned both of his parents for me on the Day of Uhud"""
"3756","Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib:\I never heard the Prophet (ﷺ) mentioning both of his parents being ransomed for anyone except for Sa'd. On the Day of Uhud"""
"3757","Narrated 'Aishah:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not sleep one night upon arriving in Al-Madinah. So he said: 'If only a righteous man would guard me tonight.'\"" She said: \""So we were like that"""
"3758","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Zalim Al-Mazini:that Sa'eed bin Zaid bin 'Amr bin Nufail said: \I bear witness for nine people"""
"3759","Narrated 'Abdul-Muttalib bin Rabi'ah bin Al-Harith bin 'Abdul-Muttalib:\\n"
"3760","so he said: 'What has angered you?' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what is it with us and the Quraish, whenever they meet one another it is with glad faces, and when they meet us they meet us with other than that?' He said: So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) became angry, until his face reddened, then he said: 'By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! Faith does not enter a man's heart until he loves you for the sake of Allah, and for the sake of His Messenger.' Then he said: 'O people! Whoever harms my uncle, he has harmed me, for indeed, a man's uncle is not but the Sinw (two or three palm trees will come from a single root, so each is called a Sinw. A man's uncle is like that to his father. That is, he is like his father) of his father. \\nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 3758 Arabic Hadees: 3758\""3761"""
"3761","Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah narrated to us from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to come out to his Companions from the Muhajirun and the Ansar while they were sitting, among them Abu Bakr and Umar. None of them would raise his gaze to him except Abu Bakr and Umar; they would look at him and he would look at them, and they would smile at him and he would smile at them. Abu Isa said: This is a Gharib hadith; we do not know it except from the hadith of al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah. Some have spoken about al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah."
"3762","Umar ibn Isma'il ibn Mujalid narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Maslamah narrated to us from Isma'il ibn Ummayah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out one day and entered the mosque, and Abu Bakr and Umar were with him, one on his right and the other on his left, and he was holding their hands, and he said: ""Thus shall we be raised on the Day of Resurrection."" Abu Isa said: This is a Gharib hadith. And Sa'id ibn Maslamah is not considered strong by them. This hadith has also been narrated from other routes from Nafi from Ibn Umar."
"3763","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Al-'Abbas is the uncle of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"""
"3764","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to Al-'Abbas: 'On the night of Monday"""
"3765","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I saw Ja'far flying in Paradise with the angels"""
"3766","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\None has put on sandals - nor worn them"""
"3767","Narrated Al-Bara bin 'Azib:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said to Ja'far bin Abi Talib: \You share similarity with me in appearance and in character"""
"3768","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\I used to ask a man from among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) concerning Ayat of the Qur'an which I would be more knowledgeable about than him"""
"3769","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\We used to call Ja'far bin Abi Talib the Father of the Poor"""
"3770","Narrated Abu Sa'eed:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Al-Hasan and Al-Husain are the chiefs of the youths of Paradise"""
"3771","Narrated Usamah bin Zaid:\I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) one night concerning some need"""
"3772","Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Abu Nu'm:that a man from the people of Al-'Iraq asked Ibn 'Umar about the blood of a gnat that gets on the clothes. Ibn 'Umar said \Look at this one"""
"3773","Narrated Abu Bakrah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ascended the Minbar and said: ""Indeed, this son of mine is a chief, Allah shall bring peace between two [tremendous] parties through his hands"
"3774","Narrated Anas bin Malik:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked: \Which of the people of your house are most beloved to you?\"" He said: \""Al-Hasan and Al-Husain.\"" And he used to say to Fatimah: \""Call my two sons for me so that I may smell them.\"" And he would hug them"""
"3775","Narrated Abu Bakrah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ascended the Minbar and said: \Indeed"""
"3776","Narrated Buraidah:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was delivering a Khutbah to us when Al-Hasan and Al-Husain [peace be upon them] came"""
"3777","Narrated Ya'la bin Murrah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Husain is from me"""
"3778","Narrated Anas bin Malik:\None of them used to resemble the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) more than Al-Hasan bin 'Ali"""
"3779","Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Al-Muqri’ narrated to us, from Haywah ibn Shurayh, from Bakr ibn ‘Amr, from Mushrih ibn Ha‘an, from ‘Uqbah ibn ‘Amir, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \n**\If there were to be a prophet after me"
"3780","Narrated Anas bin Malik:\I was with Ibn Ziyad and the head of Al-Husain was brought. He began to poke it in the nose with a stick that he had"""
"3781","Narrated 'Ali:said: \Al-Hasan is greater in resemblance to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with regards to what is between the chest and the head"""
"3782","Narrated 'Umarah bin 'Umair:\When the heads of 'Ubaidullah bin Ziyad and his companions were brought"""
"3783","Narrated Hudhaifah :\My mother asked me: 'When is your planned time - meaning with the Prophet (ﷺ)?' So I said: 'I have not had a planned time to see him since such and such time.' She rebuked me"""
"3784","Narrated by al-Hasan ibn Sabbah al-Bazzar, who said: narrated to us Zayd ibn Hubab, from Kharijah ibn Abdullah ibn Sulayman ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: informed us Yazid ibn Ruman, from Urwah, from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was sitting when we heard a commotion and the sound of children. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up, and lo, there was an Abyssinian woman performing a dance with children around her. He said, \O Aisha"
"3785","Narrated Al-Bara bin 'Azib:\I saw the Prophet (ﷺ) placing Al-Hasan bin 'Ali upon his shoulder while saying: 'O Allah"""
"3786","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was carrying Al-Hasan bin 'Ali upon his shoulder"
"3787","Narrated Al-Musayyab bin Najabah:\'Ali bin Abi Talib said: 'The Prophet SAW said: \""Indeed every Prophet is given seven select attendants\"" - or he said: \""guards\"" - \""and I was given fourteen.\"" We said: \""Who are they?\"" He said: 'Myself"""
"3788","Narrated Zaid bin Arqam, may Allah be pleased with both of them:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:""Indeed, I am leaving among you, that which if you hold fast to them, you shall not be misguided after me. One of them is greater than the other: The Book of Allah is a rope extended from the sky to the earth, and my family - the people of my house - and they shall not split until they meet at the Hawd, so look at how you deal with them after me"
"3789","Narrated 'Umar bin Abi Salamah - the step-son of the Prophet (ﷺ):\When these Ayat were revealed to the Prophet (ﷺ): 'Allah only wishes to remove the Rijs from you"""
"3790","Narrated Anas (may Allah be pleased him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) ascended Mount Uhud, accompanied by Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman (may Allah be pleased with them). The mountain trembled beneath them, whereupon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded it, saying: \Be firm"
"3791","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Love Allah for what He nourishes you with of His Blessings"""
"3792","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The most merciful of my nation to my nation is Abu Bakr"""
"3793","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The most merciful of my nation to my nation is Abu Bakr"""
"3794","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to Ubayy bin Ka'b: \Indeed Allah ordered me to recite to you: Those who disbelieve were not going to... (98:1) He said: \""And He named me?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" So he wept"""
"3795","Narrated Ubayy bin Ka'b:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him: \Indeed"""
"3796","Narrated Qatadah:that Anas bin Malik said: \Four gathered the Qur'an during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"""
"3797","Narrated Abu Hurairah:narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \What an excellent man is Abu Bakr"""
"3798","Narrated Hudhaifah bin Al-Yaman:that Al-'Aqib and As-Sayyid (two of the leaders of the Christians of Najran) came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: \Send with us your trustworthy one.\"" He said: \""I shall send with you a trustworthy one who is truly a trustworthy one.\"" So the people desired that"""
"3799","Salih ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: Abu Awanah narrated to us from Uthman ibn Abd Allah ibn Mawhab, that a man from the people of Egypt performed Hajj to the House and saw a group sitting. He said: ""Who are these?"" They said: ""Quraysh."" He said: ""Who is this old man?"" They said: ""Ibn Umar."" He came to him and said: ""I want to ask you about something; tell me, I adjure you by Allah, by the sanctity of this House: Do you know that Uthman fled on the day of Uhud?"" He said: ""Yes."" He said: ""Do you know that he was absent from the Pledge of Ridwan and did not witness it?"" He said: ""Yes."" He said: ""Do you know that he was absent on the day of Badr and did not witness it?"" He said: ""Yes."" He said: ""Allahu Akbar."" Ibn Umar said to him: ""Come, let me explain to you what you asked about. As for his flight on the day of Uhud, I bear witness that Allah has pardoned him and forgiven him. As for his absence on the day of Badr, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with him — or under his care — and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'You have the reward of a man who witnessed Badr and his share.' And he commanded him to stay behind with her, and she was ill. As for his absence from the Pledge of Ridwan, if there had been anyone more honored in the valley of Makkah than Uthman, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would have sent him instead of Uthman. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Uthman to Makkah, and the Pledge of Ridwan occurred after Uthman had gone to Makkah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said with his right hand: 'This is the hand of Uthman.' And he struck it against his own hand and said: 'This is for Uthman' (may Allah be pleased with him). He said to him: 'Go with this now.'"" Abu Isa said: This is a Hasan Sahih hadith."
"3800","Narrated 'Ali:that 'Ammar bin Yasir came seeking permission to enter upon the Prophet (ﷺ) so he said: 'Permit him"
"3801","Narrated by Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari, who said: Shadhan al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, from Sinan ibn Harun al-Burjumi, from Kulaib ibn Wa'il, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned a tribulation (fitnah) and said: \In it"
"3802","except that he choose the one with more guidance in it. \\nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 3799 Arabic Hadees: 3799\""3803"""
"3803","Ahmad ibn Abda al-Dabbi narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from Ayyub, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, who said: I went out with the Prophet ﷺ and he entered a garden of the Ansar and relieved himself. He said to me: ""O Abu Musa, guard the door for me; let no one enter upon me except by permission."" A man came and knocked on the door. I said: ""Who is this?"" He said: ""Abu Bakr."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, this is Abu Bakr asking permission."" He said: ""Permit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise."" He entered and I gave him glad tidings of Paradise. Another man came and knocked. I said: ""Who is this?"" He said: ""Umar."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, this is Umar asking permission."" He said: ""Open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise."" I opened the door, he entered, and I gave him glad tidings of Paradise. Another man came and knocked. I said: ""Who is this?"" He said: ""Uthman."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, this is Uthman asking permission."" He said: ""Open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise on account of a trial that will befall him."" Abu Isa said: This is a Hasan Sahih hadith. It has been narrated from other routes from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi. In the chapter there is also from Jabir and Ibn Umar."
"3804","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no one more truthful"""
"3805","Narrated Abu Dharr:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no one more truthful in speech"""
"3806","Narrated 'Abdul-Malik bin 'Umair:from the nephew of 'Abdullah bin Salam who said: \When they were about to kill 'Uthman"""
"3807","Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Yazid:""We came to Hudhaifah and said: 'Inform us of the closest to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in guidance and conduct, so that we may take from him and hear from him.' He said: 'The closest of the people in guidance, conduct, and character used to be 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud, until he would hide from us in his house. And the guarded ones (guarded by Allah from straying in word and deed) from the Companions of Muhammad (ﷺ) know that Ibn Umm 'Abd (a nickname for 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud) is from among the most intimately close to Allah of them"
"3808","Narrated Ibn Mas'ud:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Take as examples the two after me from my Companions"""
"3809","It was narrated to us by Sufyan ibn Waki', it was narrated to us by my father, from Israel; and it was narrated to us by Muhammad ibn Isma'il, it was narrated to us by 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa, from Israel, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara' ibn 'Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said to 'Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him): \You are from me"
"3810","Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Yazid:\We came to Hudhaifah and said: 'Inform us of the closest to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in guidance and conduct"""
"3811","Narrated 'Ali:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \If I was going to appoint anyone of them as a leader without any consultation"""
"3812","Narrated 'Ali:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \If I was going to appoint anyone as a leader without any consultation"""
"3813","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Take the Qur'an from four: From Ibn Mas'ud"""
"3814","It was narrated to us by Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan al-Baghdadi, who said: It was narrated to us by Ali ibn Qadam, who said: It was narrated to us by Ali ibn Salih ibn Hayy, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Jumayy ibn Umayr al-Taymi, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with both of them), who said:\n\n\The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) established bonds of brotherhood among his Companions. Then Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) came with his eyes flowing with tears and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"
"3815","**Sufyān ibn Wakīʿ narrated to us, saying:** ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us, from ʿĪsā ibn ʿUmar, from al-Suddī, from Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه, who said:\n\n\A bird was brought to the Prophet ﷺ"
"3816","**Narrator:** Khālid ibn Aslam al-Baghdādī\n\n**Chain:** Khālid ibn Aslam al-Baghdādī narrated to us: he said, al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl narrated to us: he said, ʿAwf informed us, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn Hind al-Jamalī, who said:\n\n**Hadith:** ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Whenever I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)"
"3817","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:\We called Zaid bin Harithah nothing but 'Zaid bin Muhammad' until the Qur'an was revealed (ordering): Call them by their fathers"""
"3818","**Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Mismar, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:**\n\nMu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan appointed Sa'd (as governor) and said to him, \What prevents you from reviling Abu Turab?\"" He (Sa'd) said: \""As for what I have mentioned — three things which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said (concerning 'Ali) — I shall never revile him"
"3819","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent and army and put Usamah bin Zaid in charge of them. So the people contested his leadership"
"3820","**Narrated 'Ali ibn al-Mundhir al-Kufi:** He said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) called for 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) on the day of Ta'if and held a private conversation with him. The people remarked, \How long his private conversation with his cousin lasted!\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: **\""I did not hold a private conversation with him"
"3821","Narrated by Ali ibn al-Mundhir, who said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us from Salim ibn Abi Hafsah from 'Atiyyah from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said to Ali, peace be upon him: \O Ali"
"3822","Narrated Usamah bin Zaid:\I was sitting [with the Prophet (ﷺ)] when 'Ali and Al-'Abbas came seeking permission to enter. They said: 'O Usamah"""
"3823","Narrated Jarir bin 'Abdullah:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) never screened me since I accepted Islam"""
"3824","Narrated Jarir:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) never screened me since I accepted Islam"""
"3825","Narrated Abu Jahdam:from Ibn 'Abbas that he saw Jibra'il (AS)"
"3826","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) supplicated for me that Allah should give me Al-Hukm (knowledge"""
"3827","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) pulled me close to him and said: 'O Allah"""
"3828","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:\I had a dream in which I saw as if there was a piece of silk in my hand"""
"3829","**Muḥammad ibn Bashshār and Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us, both saying:** Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, saying: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, from Abū Ḥamzah — a man from the Anṣār — who said:\n\n\I heard Zayd ibn Arqam رضي الله عنه say: **'The first to embrace Islam was ʿAlī (ibn Abī Ṭālib).'\""**\n\nʿAmr ibn Murrah said: **\""I mentioned this to Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī"
"3830","Narrated Anas bin Malik:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by"""
"3831","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: \O possessor of two ears!\"" (One of the narrators) Abu Usamah said: 'He only meant it as a joke"""
"3832","Abū Saʿīd al-Ashajj narrated to us, saying: Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, from Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbbād ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, from his grandfather ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Zubayr"
"3833","Narrated Anas [may Allah be pleased with him]:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave me my Kunyah because of a plant that I used to care for"""
"3834","Narrated Thabit Al-Bunani:\Anas bin Malik said to me: 'O Thabit"""
"3835","Abū Saʿīd al-Ashajj narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Manṣūr al-ʿAnazī narrated to us from ʿUqbah ibn ʿAlqamah al-Yashkurī, who said: I heard ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allāh be pleased with him) say: \I heard with my own ears from the mouth of the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) as he said: 'Ṭalḥah and al-Zubayr are my neighbours in Paradise.'\"" He (the narrator) said: \""This is a *gharīb* hadith; we do not know it except through this chain.\"""""
"3836","Narrated Abu Khaldah:\I said to Abu Al-'Aliyah: '(Did) Anas heard from the Prophet (ﷺ)?' He said: 'He served him for ten years"""
"3837","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and spread out my garment next to him"""
"3838","Narrated by Ahmad ibn Mani', who said: narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr, who said: narrated to us Zaidah, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Indeed"
"3839","Narrated Al-Walid bin 'Abdur-Rahman:that Ibn 'Umar said to Abu Hurairah: \You used to stick to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) most out of all of us"""
"3840","Narrated Malik bin Abi 'Amir:\A man came to Talhah bin 'Ubaidullah and said: 'O Abu Muhammad"""
"3841","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\The Prophet (ﷺ) said to me: 'Who are you from?' I said: 'From Daws.' He said: 'I did not used think there was anyone from Daws in whom there was good"""
"3842","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) with some dates and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"""
"3843","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Rafi':\I said to Abu Hurairah: 'Why were you given the Kunyah Abu Hurairah?' He said: 'Do you not fear me?'\"" He said: \""Indeed"""
"3844","Narrated Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him] :\There is none with more Ahadith from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) than I"""
"3845","Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Abu 'Umairah - and he was one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ):from the Prophet (ﷺ)"
"3846","Narrated Abu Idris Al-Khawlani:\When 'Umar bin Al-Khattab removed 'Umair bin Sa'd as governor of Hims"""
"3847","Narrated 'Uqbah bin 'Amir:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The people submitted while 'Amr bin Al-'As believed"""
"3848","Narrated Talhah bin 'Ubaidullah:\I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'Indeed"""
"3849","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\We camped with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) at a place"""
"3850","Narrated Al-Bara:\A garment of silk was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) so they began to marvel at its softness"""
"3851","Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to me, not riding a mule nor a Birdhawn (a type of Turkish horse)"
"3852","Narrated Jabir:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) supplicated for forgiveness for me on the Night of the Camel, twenty-five times"
"3853","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Dawraqi, who was informed by Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, from al-Jurayri, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, who said: I asked 'Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): \Which of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was most beloved to him?\"" She replied: \""Abu Bakr.\"" I asked: \""Then who?\"" She said: \""Then 'Umar.\"" I asked: \""Then who?\"" She said: \""Then Abu 'Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah.\"" I asked: \""Then who?\"" She remained silent."""
"3854","Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to me"""
"3855","Narrated Jabir:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) supplicated for forgiveness for me on the Night of the Camel"""
"3856","Narrated Khabbab:\We emigrated with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"""
"3857","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \How many are there with dishevelled hair"""
"3858","Narrated Abu Musa:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \O Abu Musa! You have been given a Mizmar among the Mazamir of the family of Dawud"""
"3859","Narrated Sahl bin Sa'd:\We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while he was excavating the trench"""
"3860","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would say: \O Allah! There is no life but the life of the Hereafter! So honor the Ansar and the Emigrants"""
"3861","Narrated Talhah bin Khirash:\I heard Jabir bin 'Abdullah saying: 'I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) saying: \""The Fire shall not touch the Muslim who saw me"""
"3862","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The best generation is my generation"""
"3863","Narrated Jabir:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \None of those who gave the pledge under the tree shall enter the Fire"""
"3864","Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Do not abuse my Companions"""
"3865","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mughaffal:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \(Fear) Allah! (Fear) Allah regarding my Companions! Do not make them objects of insults after me. Whoever loves them"""
"3866","**Narrated by 'Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Baṣrī al-'Ammī**, who said: **Wahb ibn Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim** narrated to us, who said: **My father** narrated to us, from **Muḥammad ibn Abī Ya'qūb**, from **'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Nu'm**, that **a man from the people of Iraq asked Ibn 'Umar** (may Allāh be pleased with them both) **about the blood of mosquitoes that stains clothing**. Thereupon, **Ibn 'Umar** (may Allāh be pleased with him) said:\n\n*\Look at this man! He asks about the blood of mosquitoes"
"3867","Abū Saʿīd al-Ashajj narrated to us, saying: Abū Khālid al-Aḥmar narrated to us, saying: Ruzayn narrated to us, saying: Salmā narrated to me, saying:\n\nI entered upon Umm Salamah (may Allāh be pleased with her) while she was weeping. I said, \What causes you to weep?\"" She said"
"3868","Abū Saʿīd al-Ashajj narrated to us, saying: ʿUqbah ibn Khālid narrated to us, saying: Yūsuf ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to me, that he heard Anas ibn Mālik (may Allāh be pleased with him) say:\n\nThe Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked: \Which member of your household is most beloved to you?\"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: \""Al-Ḥasan and Al-Ḥusayn.\""\n\nHe (peace and blessings be upon him) would also say to Fāṭimah (may Allāh be pleased with her): \""Bring me my two sons.\"" He would then smell them and embrace them.\n\nThis is a *gharīb* (uncommon) hadith from this chain of narration"
"3869","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \If you see those who abuse my Companions"""
"3870","Narrated Zaid bin Arqam:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to 'Ali, Fatimah, Al-Hasan and Al-Husain: \I am at war with whoever makes war with you"
"3871","Narrated Buraidah:\The most beloved of women to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was Fatimah and from the men was 'Ali"""
"3872","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Az-Zubair:that 'Ali mentioned the daughter of Abu Jahl (for marriage)"
"3873","Narrated Zaid bin Arqam:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to 'Ali"
"3874","Narrated Umm Salamah:\The Prophet (ﷺ) put a garment over Al-Hasan"""
"3875","Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani' ibn Hani', from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: al-Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him) most resembled the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) from the chest upward, while al-Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him) most resembled the Prophet (peace be upon him) from that point downward. This is a hasan gharib hadith."
"3876","Narrated Umm Salamah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called Fatimah on the Day of the Conquest (of Makkah) and he spoke to her"
"3877","Narrated Jumai' bin 'Umair At-Taimi:\I entered along with my uncle upon 'Aishah and she was asked: 'Who among people was the most beloved to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?' She said: 'Fatimah.' So it was said: 'From the men?' She said: 'Her husband"""
"3878","Narrated 'Aishah:\I was not jealous of any wife of the Prophet (ﷺ) as I was jealous of Khadijah"""
"3879","Narrated 'Aishah:\I did not envy any woman as I envied Khadijah - and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not marry me except after she had died - that was because the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave her glad tidings of a house in Paradise made of Qasab"""
"3880","Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The best of its women is Khadijah bint Khuwailid"""
"3881","Narrated Anas [may Allah be pleased with him]:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Sufficient for you among the women of mankind are Mariam bint 'Imran"""
"3882","Narrated 'Aishah:\The people used to give their gifts [to the Prophet (ﷺ)] on 'Aishah's day.\"" She said: \""So my companions gathered with Umm Salamah and they said 'O Umm Salamah! The people give their gifts on 'Aishah's day"""
"3883","Narrated 'Aishah:that Jibril came to the Prophet (ﷺ) with her image upon a piece of green silk cloth"
"3884","Narrated 'Aishah [may Allah be pleased with her]:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \O 'Aishah! Here is Jibril and he is giving Salam to you.\"" She said: \""I said: 'And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah"""
"3885","Narrated 'Aishah:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: 'Indeed Jibril gives his Salam to you.' So I said: 'And upon him be peace and Allah's Mercy [and His blessings]"""
"3886","Narrated Abu Musa:\Never was a Hadith unclear to us - the Companions of the Messenger of Allah - and we asked 'Aishah"""
"3887","Narrated Musa bin Talhah:\I have not seen anyone clearer (in speech) than 'Aishah"""
"3888","Narrated 'Amr bin Al-'As:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) appointed him as a leader of the army of Dhatis-Salasil. He said: \So I went to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Who is the most beloved to you among the people?' He said: ''Aishah.' I said: 'From the men?' He said: 'Her father"""
"3889","Narrated 'Amr bin Al-'As:that he said to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): \Who is the most beloved of the people to you?\"" He said: \""'Aishah.\"" He said: \""From the men?\"" He said: \""Her farther"""
"3890","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The virtue of 'Aishah over women is like the virtue of Tharid over all other foods"""
"3891","Narrated 'Amr bin Ghalib:that a man spoke negatively of 'Aishah before 'Ammar bin Yasir so he said: \Be gone as one despicable and rejected! Do you insult the beloved of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?"""
"3892","Narrated 'Ammar bin Yasir:\She is his wife in the world and in the Hereafter.\"" - meaning: 'Aishah [may Allah be pleased with her]"""
"3893","Narrated Anas [May Allah be pleased with him]:\It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Who is the most beloved of the people to you?' He said: ''Aishah.' It was said: 'From the men?' He said: 'Her father"""
"3894","Narrated by Muhammad ibn Bashshar, who said: narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, who said: narrated to us Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani' ibn Hani', from Ali"
"3895","Narrated Safiyyah bint Huyai:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered upon me and some words had reached me from Hafsah and 'Aishah. So I mentioned it to him. So he said: 'Why did you not say: \""And how are you two better than me"""
"3896","Narrated Umm Salamah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called for Fatimah in the Year of the Conquest to speak to her"
"3897","Narrated Anas:said: \It reached Safiyyah that Hafsah said: 'The daughter of a Jew' so she wept. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) entered upon her while she was crying"""
"3898","Narrated 'Aishah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The best of you is the best to his wives"""
"3899","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \No one should convey to me anything regarding any of my Companions"""
"3900","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \No one should convey to me anything regarding anyone"""
"3901","Narrated Ubayy bin Ka'b:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him: \Indeed Allah has ordered me to recite the Qur'an to you.\"" So he recited to him: \""Those who disbelieved were not going to... (98:1) and he recited in it: \""Indeed the religion with Allah is that which is Hanafiyyah"""
"3902","Narrated Ubayy bin Ka'b:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \If it were not for the Hijrah"""
"3903","Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī (may Allāh be pleased with him) said: \My brother and I came from Yemen"
"3904","Narrated Anas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gathered a group of people from the Ansar and said: \Come"""
"3905","Narrated by Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: Sa'id al-Harrani informed us, who said: Zuhayr narrated to us, who said: Mansur narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali"
"3906","Narrated Abu Talhah:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: 'Convey my Salam to your people"""
"3907","Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Indeed my elite"""
"3908","Narrated Sa'd:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever wishes to humiliate the Quraish then Allah will humiliate him"""
"3909","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\The Prophet (ﷺ) said to me: 'A man who believes in Allah and the Last Day does not hate the Ansar"""
"3910","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The Ansar are my close ones and my elite. Indeed the people shall increase and they shall dwindle"""
"3911","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \O Allah! You made the first of the Quraish taste punishment"""
"3912","Narrated Anas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \O Allah forgive the Ansar and the children of the Ansar"""
"3913","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Shall I inform you of the best houses of the Ansar"""
"3914","Narrated Abu Usaid As-Sa'idi:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The Best houses of the Ansar are the houses of Banu An-Najjar"""
"3915","Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The best house of the Ansar is Banu An-Najjar"""
"3916","Narrated Jabir [bin 'Abdullah]:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The best of the Ansar are Banu 'Abdul-Ashhal"""
"3917","Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib:\We departed with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) until he was at Harrah As-Suqya which belonged to Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Bring me water for Wudu.' So he performed Wudu"""
"3918","Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib and Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whatever is between my house and my Minbar is a garden from the gardens of Paradise"""
"3919","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \What is between my house and my Minbar is a garden from the gardens of Paradise.\"" And with this chain"""
"3920","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever is able to die in Al-Madinah"""
"3921","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that a freed a slave girl of his came to him"
"3922","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The last of the cities of Islam to be destroyed is Al-Madinah"""
"3923","Narrated Jabir:that a Bedouin gave the pledge to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) for Islam"
"3924","Narrated Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab:that Abu Hurairah used to say: \If I saw hyenas roaming in Al-Madinah"""
"3925","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that (mount) Uhud appeared to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) so he said: \This mountain loves us and we love it. O Allah! Indeed Ibrahim made Makkah sacred"""
"3926","Narrated Jarir bin 'Abdullah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Indeed Allah has revealed to me that: Whichever of these three places you go to will be the place of your emigration: Al-Madinah"""
"3927","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \No one is patient with the difficulties and hardships of Al-Madinah"""
"3928","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Adi bin Hamra [Az-Zuhri]:\I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) standing at Al-Hazwarah"""
"3929","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said about Makkah: \How sweet of a land you are and how dear you are to me"""
"3930","Narrated Salman:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: 'O Salman! Do not detest me and thereby leave your religion.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! How could I detest you while Allah guided us by you.' He said: 'You will detest the Arabs and thereby detest me"""
"3931","Narrated 'Uthman bin 'Affan:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever cheats the Arabs"""
"3932","Narrated Muhammad bin Abi Razin:that his mother said: \If someone died from the Arabs it would be hard upon Umm Al-Harir so it was said to her: 'We see that if a man from the Arabs dies it is hard upon you.' She said: 'I heard my Mawla say that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""From the (signs of) coming of the Hour is the destruction of the Arabs.\"" Muhammad bin Abi Razin said: \""And her Mawla was Talhah bin Malik"""
"3933","Narrated Umm Sharik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The people will flee from the Dajjal such that they will go to the mountains.\"" Umm Sharik said: \""O Messenger of Allah! Where will the Arabs be that day?\"" He said: \""They will be few"""
"3934","Narrated Samurah bin Jundab:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Sam was the father of Arabs"""
"3935","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\Al-'Ajam (non-Arabs) were mentioned before the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) so the Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'I am supported more by them"""
"3936","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when Surat Al-Jumu'ah was revealed"""
"3937","Narrated Zaid bin Thabit [may Allah be pleased with him]:that the Prophet (ﷺ) looked towards Yemen and said: \O Allah direct their hearts and bless us in our Sa' and our Mudd"""
"3938","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The people of Yemen have come to you. They are weaker in heart and softer in understanding"""
"3939","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Leadership is among the Quraish"""
"3941","Narrated Anas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Al-Azd is Allah's lion upon the earth"""
"3942","Narrated Anas:\If we are not from Al-Azd then we are not from the people"""
"3943","**Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: Al-Layth narrated to us, from Hishām ibn Saʿd, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:**\n\nWe encamped with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) at a certain resting place. The people began to pass by, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would say: **\Who is this"
"3944","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Aslam"""
"3945","Narrated Jabir:\They said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Thaqif are razing us with their arrows"""
"3946","Narrated 'Imran bin Husain:\The Prophet (ﷺ) died while he was having trouble with three tribes: Thaqif"""
"3947","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \In Thaqif there is a liar and a destroyer"""
"3948","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that a Bedouin gave a young female camel as a gift to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"3949","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\A man from Banu Fazarah gave a gift to the Prophet (ﷺ) of she-camel from his camels which they had taken at Al-Ghabah. So he reciprocated for it with something in return"""
"3950","Narrated 'Amir bin Abi 'Amir Al-Ash'ari:from his father who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Blessed are the tribes of Al-Asad and Al-Ash'arun"""
"3951","Narrated by Abdullah ibn Abi Ziyad, who said: Sayyar narrated to us, who said: Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, who said: Thabit and 'Ali ibn Zaid narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n\How many a disheveled"
"3952","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Dinar:similar to Shu'bah (#3948) and he added: \And 'Usayyah has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger"""
"3953","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \By the One in Whose Hand is Muhammad's soul! Ghifar"""
"3954","Narrated 'Imran bin Husain:that a group from Banu Tamim came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) so he said: \Have glad tidings O Banu Tamim.\"" They said: \""You have given us glad tidings"""
"3955","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""People should stop boasting about their fathers who have died, while they are but coals of Hell, or they will be more humiliated with Allah than the dung beetle who rolls dung with his nose. Indeed Allah has removed the pride of Jahiliyyah from you, and its boasting about lineage. [Indeed a person is either] a pious believer, or a miserable sinner. And people are all the children of Adam, and Adam was [created] from dust"
"3956","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \O Allah bless us in our Sham! O Allah bless us in our Yemen.\"" They said: \""And in our Najd\"" He said: \""O Allah bless us in our Sham and bless us in our Yemen.\"" They said: \""And in our Najd\"" He said: \""Earthquakes are there"""
